. 
Sharing 
Sharing finds its place naturally. 
When pages are shared, working sets will overlap. If 
Arden's [7] suggestion concerning program structure 4 is 
ollowed, sharing of data can be accomplished without 
modification of the regime of Figure 7. If a page is in at 
east one working set, the "use bits" in the page table 
ntry will be ON and the page will not be removed. To 
revent anomalies, the checker must not be permitted to 
